    ;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;EBOLA MODEL MODS;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
    ;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;EBOLA SURVIVAL NEEDS;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; We model survival in its subgroups of food, sleep, financial, and health
;; FOOD includes water and is procured as a day activity at markets or stores, getting food increases health but damages finances

;; SLEEP is only replenished by sleeping (at home, at night)

;; FINANCIAL survival is replenished by working (in mine, agriculture, shop, hospital, or church) not housework
;;;;a person who is sick and getting treatment at home or hospital depleats financial survival

;; HEALTH ( maybe be redundant )
;;;;as workers in Mongbwalu are not storing large amounts of food at home and need to work for daily survival, the available rations are always NULL or the amount of capital is minimal TBD
;;;;only procuring food replenishes Health
;;;;food in hospital is not a given, so if a patient is being treated, their health satisfaction is also low - this links to people's desire to visit relatives in hospitals

;;financial stability is not present explicitly in Ebola model

